---
import StoreBadges from '../components/StoreBadges.astro';
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Is Recur a Fitbod alternative?',
    answer:
      'If you want a free tier that never expires and an app that eases you back in after a break instead of picking up where you left off, yes. If you want the broadest possible exercise library for six-day-a-week gym training, Fitbod may fit you better.',
  },
];
---

<ContentPage
  title="Recur vs Fitbod | Recur"
  description="How Recur compares to Fitbod: free tier, break re-entry, and pain routing."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: faqs.map(faq => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: faq.question,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.answer },
    })),
  })} />

  <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-2">Recur vs Fitbod</h1>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-12">A straight comparison, not a sales pitch.</p>

  <div class="max-w-none space-y-10 text-foreground">
    <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      Fitbod is a well-known name in adaptive workout apps, with a large exercise library and
      gym-equipment support. If you're comparing it to Recur, here's where we're actually different,
      not a list of reasons to avoid them.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Where Recur is different</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Three workouts a week are free, forever. Not a trial.</li>
        <li>Flag a knee or shoulder and Recur routes around it automatically, no separate injury mode to configure.</li>
        <li>Take a few weeks off and Recur eases you back in instead of resuming at your old volume.</li>
        <li>Built for home equipment: dumbbells, kettlebells, bodyweight. No gym required.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Who Recur isn't for</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        If you train six days a week across a full gym and want the widest possible exercise
        library and machine variety, Fitbod's broader catalog may suit you better. Recur is built
        for people rebuilding a habit that keeps slipping, not for chasing PRs across every machine
        in the building.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">FAQ</h2>
      {faqs.map(faq => (
        <div class="mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">{faq.question}</h3>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">{faq.answer}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="pt-6">
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Three workouts a week, free, forever. See for yourself.
      </p>
      <StoreBadges location="vs_fitbod_page" />
    </section>
  </div>
</ContentPage>
